arched in UTC for November 9 and 10, I noticed events on November 10 that I didn't want. I have to confirm that for November 9, there are no upcoming events, but there seems to be some confusion due to the email timestamp. So, I'll clarify for the user.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Addressing scheduling discrepancies**\\n\\nIt's important to clarify the scheduling issues here. I should say something like, \\\"There are no calendar events for Monday, Nov 9, in the Pacific timezone, but on Tuesday, Nov 10, UTC, I see a team standup and the Q3 planning review.\\\" I need to address the potential confusion caused by Dana's email about bringing the budget sheet for the review, which is set for Nov 10 UTC, so I’ll include a message about this mismatch. I'll draft that message carefully.\"},{\"type\":\"summary_text\",\"text\":\"**Confirming event timezone and date**\\n\\nOkay, so the calendar starts with a timezone field in UTC, which is good. I need to acknowledge the current date from the local system, confirming that tomorrow, Mon Nov 9, is indeed a Monday in 2026. Since the user is in the PST timezone, I should mention that I'm basing this on a Pacific OS environment. I've checked the command called to list the calendar events, and it came back empty. I'll finalize this with a concise draft confirmation.\"}]},{\"id\":\"msg_0c008018e11fdb7f016af12a51184c87d0895e7762cf733b2e\",\"type\":\"message\",\"status\":\"completed\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"output_text\",\"annotations\":[],\"logprobs\":[],\"text\":\"- **Tomorrow, Mon Nov 9 (Pacific):** I found no calendar events.\\n- **Dana did email** asking you to bring the latest budget sheet to the planning review, especially the Q3 travel line. I found the **Q3 Budget** spreadsheet: [Open the sheet](https://docs.example.test/spreadsheets/d/f-budget).\\n- I also see a **Q3 planning review** with Dana on **Tue, Nov 10, 14:00–15:00 UTC** in Room 4, plus **Team standup** at 09:00–09:15 UTC. Dana’s “tomorrow” note appears to refer to that Nov 10 review.\\n- I drafted a reply with the sheet link and left it **unsent**.\"}],\"phase\":\"final_answer\",\"role\":\"assistant\"}],\"parallel_tool_calls\":true,\"presence_penalty\":0.0,\"previous_response_id\":null,\"prompt_cache_key\":\"01a1be0c-a70e-74ee-a458-65227b73e9e9\",\"prompt_cache_retention\":\"24h\",\"reasoning\":{\"context\":\"all_turns\",\"effort\":\"medium\",\"mode\":\"standard\",\"summary\":\"detailed\"},\"safety_identifier\":null,\"service_tier\":\"default\",\"store\":false,\"temperature\":1.0,\"text\":{\"format\":{\"type\":\"text\"},\"verbosity\":\"medium\"},\"tool_choice\":\"auto\",\"tool_usage\":{\"image_gen\":{\"input_tokens\":0,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"image_tokens\":0,\"text_tokens\":0},\"output_tokens\":0,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"image_tokens\":0,\"text_tokens\":0},\"total_tokens\":0},\"web_search\":{\"num_requests\":0}},\"tools\":[{\"type\":\"function\",\"description\":\"Execute a bash command in the current working directory. Returns stdout and stderr. Output is truncated to last 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). If truncated, full output is saved to a temp file. Optionally provide a timeout in seconds.\\n\\nmail, calendar, drive are not tools you call directly: reach them from bash with the `tools` command. `tools list` shows them, `tools list <tool> --schema` a tool's commands and arguments, `tools call <tool>.<command> --json -` with the arguments on stdin in a quoted heredoc (`<<'JSON'`), so quotes in them need no escaping, makes one call, and `tools run` with a script on stdin (`await tools.<tool>.<command>({...})`) makes several.\",\"name\":\"bash\",\"output_schema\":null,\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"command\",\"timeout\"],\"properties\":{\"command\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Shell command to execute\"},\"timeout\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Timeout in seconds (optional, no default timeout)\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}]}},\"additionalProperties\":false},\"strict\":true},{\"type\":\"function\",\"description\":\"Read the contents of a file. Supports text files and images (jpg, png, gif, webp, bmp). Images are sent as attachments. For text files, output is truncated to 2000 lines or 50KB (whichever is hit first). Use offset/limit for large files. When you need the full file, continue with offset until complete.\",\"name\":\"read\",\"output_schema\":null,\"parameters\":{\"type\":\"object\",\"required\":[\"path\",\"offset\",\"limit\"],\"properties\":{\"path\":{\"type\":\"string\",\"description\":\"Path to the file to read (relative or absolute)\"},\"offset\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Line number to start reading from (1-indexed)\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}]},\"limit\":{\"anyOf\":[{\"type\":\"number\",\"description\":\"Maximum number of lines to read\"},{\"type\":\"null\"}]}},\"additionalProperties\":false},\"strict\":true}],\"top_logprobs\":0,\"top_p\":0.98,\"truncation\":\"disabled\",\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":6420,\"input_tokens_details\":{\"cache_write_tokens\":815,\"cached_tokens\":5602},\"output_tokens\":1174,\"output_tokens_details\":{\"reasoning_tokens\":1010},\"total_tokens\":7594},\"user\":null,\"metadata\":{}},\"sequence_number\":463}\n\n"
